WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.770
This virus wears a stolen coat.

2
00:00:02.820 --> 00:00:08.420
Its envelope is a lipid bilayer, taken
from the membrane of a cell it infected.

3
00:00:08.470 --> 00:00:12.740
Inside: two copies of its
genes, written in RNA,

4
00:00:12.790 --> 00:00:15.270
with enzymes packed in alongside.

5
00:00:15.320 --> 00:00:21.050
Its target: helper T cells, the cells
that coordinate the immune response.

6
00:00:21.100 --> 00:00:26.100
So how does one virus turn the body's own
defenders into factories that make more

7
00:00:26.150 --> 00:00:27.190
of it?

8
00:00:27.240 --> 00:00:30.790
In this mission, you'll
take an HIV particle apart,

9
00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:32.490
layer by layer.

10
00:00:32.540 --> 00:00:35.150
Then you'll follow it
into a helper T cell,

11
00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:38.360
from docking to new particles budding out.

12
00:00:38.410 --> 00:00:43.560
Your mission: explain how one virus
turns the body's defenders into factories

13
00:00:43.610 --> 00:00:45.010
for more of itself.
